With ES-DE, the build includes MAGISK_ES-DE_fix.zip from GammaOS Next
(https://github.com/TheGammaSqueeze/GammaOSNext), unchanged, Copyright
TheGammaSqueeze, Apache License 2.0.

On the 1.4.4 base, the build downloads and includes the Colorful (Simplified)
theme for ES-DE (https://github.com/anthonycaccese/colorful-simplified-es-de)
by ant, based on the Colorful theme by viking and faeran, under the Creative
Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 2.0 license; its README, with
the full credits, is installed with it. Its artwork credits, as the theme
gives them:

  Most artwork originally created by viking
  (https://forums.launchbox-app.com/profile/70421-viking/) & faeran
  (https://forums.launchbox-app.com/files/file/2081-colorful-bigbox-theme).
  For systems that did not exist in the Colorful set, some were sourced from
  the work done by g-spawn (https://github.com/g-spawnPL) for the ckau-book
  theme (https://github.com/CkauNui/ckau-book/tree/master), edited to add
  transparency.
  OpenBOR sprites (openbor.webp) originally created by DOA687
  (https://www.deviantart.com/doa687).
  M.U.G.E.N. sprites (mugen.webp) originally created by mpadillathespriter
  (https://www.deviantart.com/mpadillathespriter).
  EasyRPG artwork (easyrpg.webp) originally created by SeraphCircle
  (https://twitter.com/SeraphCircle).
  Doom artwork (doom.webp) originally created by azakachi-rd-17
  (https://www.deviantart.com/azakachi-rd-17).
  LowresNX artwork (lowresnx.webp) by Duimon
  (https://forums.libretro.com/t/duimon-hsm-mega-bezel-graphics-and-presets-feedback-and-updates/28146/1049).
  The base folder image used to create the All Games, Favorites, Last Played
  and Custom Collections images (auto-allgames.webp, auto-favorites.webp,
  auto-lastplayed.webp, custom-collections.webp) was sourced from Rick
  Patrick (https://www.softicons.com/designers/rick-patrick).
  The icons on the folder images were sourced from FontAwesome
  (https://fontawesome.com/search?o=r&m=free), Font Awesome Free, CC BY 4.0.

Thimsy OS's copy of the theme is changed, as noted at the end of its README:
  - the Gilroy font (Radomir Tinkov, commercial) is replaced by Urbanist
    1.330 (https://github.com/coreyhu/Urbanist), Copyright 2024 The Urbanist
    Project Authors, SIL Open Font License 1.1, installed with its OFL.txt;
  - the help bar's Akrobat Bold (Fontfabric, whose free-font license does not
    allow redistribution) is replaced by Barlow Semi Condensed Bold 1.422
    (https://github.com/jpt/barlow), Copyright 2017 The Barlow Project
    Authors, SIL Open Font License 1.1, installed with its OFL.txt;
  - theme.xml names the new font files;
  - quake.webp, a Quake Champions render (id Software) credited to noorkabir
    (imgbin.com), is removed; a replacement is needed, and until then the
    Quake system shows the theme's default picture.

On the 1.4.4 base, Barlow Semi Condensed Medium and SemiBold also replace
Nano's copies of Akrobat (/system/etc/nano_xmb/fonts/akrobat-regular.ttf and
akrobat-semibold.ttf, ES-DE's default face), with Barlow's OFL.txt beside
them.

GammaOS Nano, on the 1.4.4 base, ships:
  - the RetroArch "Monochrome" system icons from retroarch-assets
    (https://github.com/libretro/retroarch-assets), by the libretro project
    and its contributors, under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
    International license (CC BY 4.0);
  - Font Awesome 4.7.0 (https://github.com/FortAwesome/Font-Awesome), the
    font by Dave Gandy, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1;
  - Rounded M+ 1c Medium (http://jikasei.me/), Copyright 2016 The Rounded M+
    Project Authors, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1;
  - Earth maps from NASA's Blue Marble and Earth's City Lights
    (https://visibleearth.nasa.gov), by NASA Goddard Space Flight Center,
    in the public domain;
  - "Retro Arcade Game Music" by original_soundtrack (Viacheslav Starostin)
    (https://pixabay.com/music/upbeat-retro-arcade-game-music-408074/), as
    GammaEQ's preview (preview.wav), under the Pixabay Content License.
The build downloads "Computer Startup Sound Effect" by Dragon Studio
(https://pixabay.com/sound-effects/film-special-effects-computer-startup-sound-effect-312870/)
and installs it as the ES-DE home's startup sound (esde_boot.mp3), under the
Pixabay Content License.

GammaOS Nano also includes Slate, ES-DE's default theme, by the ES-DE
project, based on recalbox-multi by the Recalbox community, with graphics by
Rookervik, Bezza191 and Dan Patrick, under the Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 2.0 license (its LICENSE and CREDITS.md
are in the zip). Its fonts are Exo 2 (https://github.com/googlefonts/Exo-2.0)
by Natanael Gama, Copyright 2013 The Exo 2 Project Authors, SIL Open Font
License 1.1.

On the 1.4.4 base, Nano's emulator catalog (/system/etc/nano_xmb/daijishou)
is Daijishou's platform data (https://github.com/TapiocaFox/Daijishou),
Copyright (c) 2022 TapiocaFox (Yves Chen), MIT License.

